---
description: |
  Deduplicates HarfangLab Module Activity (`class_uid` 1005) into one event
  per time window, host, and module file. Events of other classes pass
  through unchanged.

  Each result is a Module Activity event with the OCSF aggregation
  attributes: `count` holds the number of loads, `start_time` and `end_time`
  the times of the first and last one, and `time` equals `start_time`. All
  times are epoch milliseconds, like HarfangLab's.

  The result describes the module with its complete `module.file`, including
  its hashes and signature, so another binary at the same path yields its own
  result. The base address differs between loads and doesn't appear.
  HarfangLab identifies the loading process mostly by its process ID alone.
  The result keeps the name and path of the loading process only if all
  loads came from the same one, and `unmapped.distinct_actor_pids` holds the
  number of distinct loading process IDs.

  Windows use event time from `time`, aligned to the Unix epoch, with a
  separate clock per host, so a host with a skewed clock or a backlog doesn't
  close the windows of other hosts. A window closes once its host sends an
  event past the window end plus `tolerance`, after `window` without any
  event from the host, or when the input ends. The operator drops events that
  arrive after their window closed, with a warning.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 1d
      description: Width of the deduplication windows.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: How long a window waits for late events of its host.
---

if class_uid == 1005 {
  // The outer grouping gives every host its own event-time clock and keeps
  // the device and metadata records out of the per-window state.
  group {device: device, metadata: metadata} {
    window size=$window, on=from_epoch(time * 1ms), tolerance=$tolerance,
           idle_timeout=$window {
      summarize activity_id, activity_name?, type_uid, severity_id,
        severity?, module.file, module.load_type_id?,
        module.type?, module.function_name?,
        count=count(), start_time=min(time), end_time=max(time),
        _pids=count_distinct(actor.process.pid?),
        _names=distinct(actor.process.name?),
        _name_count=count(actor.process.name?),
        _paths=distinct(actor.process.file.path?),
        _path_count=count(actor.process.file.path?)
      name = _names[0] if _names.length() == 1 and _name_count == count else null
      path = _paths[0] if _paths.length() == 1 and _path_count == count else null
      this = {
        activity_id: activity_id,
        activity_name: activity_name,
        category_uid: 1,
        class_uid: 1005,
        metadata: $group.metadata,
        severity: severity,
        severity_id: severity_id,
        time: start_time,
        start_time: start_time,
        end_time: end_time,
        count: count,
        type_uid: type_uid,
        // OCSF requires the actor, so it stays even when nothing about the
        // loading process holds for all loads.
        actor: {
          process: {
            file: {path: path} if path != null else null,
            name: name,
          },
        },
        device: $group.device,
        module: module,
        unmapped: {distinct_actor_pids: _pids},
      }
      drop_null_fields
    }
  }
}
